## 4. Figure and table (owner: `figtab-repo`, path `report/figures/`)

Exactly one figure and one table (venue V5), rendered by a script in `report/figures/` from the
files in `report/results/`, never from typed numbers.

- **Table** must show: rows LR, kNN, LR - kNN; mean accuracy and primary 95% interval for each; the
  interval method named in the caption (corrected resampled t, J = 50); which run the numbers come
  from and the identity verdict (or a pointer to the text). A labelled naive-interval column only if
  it fits.
- **Figure** must let the reader check Q1-Q2: the fold-level spread of each method's accuracy with
  its mean and 95% interval, and the paired differences d_f with their mean and 95% interval against
  a zero line. Accuracies are discrete (1/30 steps): overlap must stay visible (counts, jitter or
  per-repetition means). Single-column, compact (2-page cap). Selected k may appear here, in the
  table or in the text, as space allows.

## 5. Report (owner: `paper-repo`, path `report/`; format: `venue-repo`)

`report/report.pdf` from `report/report.tex` (pdflatex, TeX Live 2026), NeurIPS 2026 template with
the default anonymous option and the unmodified `neurips_2026.sty`, **at most two pages for the whole
PDF**, no checklist (venue V1-V7). Content: one-paragraph motivation; data provenance (OpenML 61,
sha256); design D2-D5 in a few sentences; results with the table and figure; reproducibility
(Ibex node name, job id, identity verdict at L1/L2, environment); limitations (one small dataset,
approximate intervals for dependent CV folds with possible undercoverage (Bates, Hastie & Tibshirani
2023), untuned LR, duplicates / UCI-vs-Fisher entries kept); references as verified in the `idea-repo`
brief §4 (Fisher 1936; Cover & Hart 1967; OpenML, Vanschoren et al. 2014; scikit-learn, Pedregosa et
al. 2011; Nadeau & Bengio 2003; Bouckaert & Frank 2004; Varma & Simon 2006 for nested selection;
Dietterich 1998; Bates et al. 2023; Bezdek et al. 1999), as space allows. All numbers via `\input{results/numbers.tex}` and the
figtab files; `report/README.md` maps each number to the script and result file that produced it.

